<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vocabolario degli Accademici della Crusca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1612</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vocabolario degli Accademici della Crusca was the dictionary of the Italian language published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1612 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accademia-della-crusca">Accademia della Crusca</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>. Based on the Florentine of fourteenth-century writers, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrarch">Petrarch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-boccaccio">Boccaccio</a>, it established Tuscan as the model for literary Italian and served as an example for the dictionaries of the French and Spanish academies. Revised editions followed into the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vocabolario-degli-accademici-della-crusca.jpg" alt="Vocabolario degli Accademici della Crusca" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Villa_di_castello,_sede_dell%27accademia_della_crusca,_sala_delle_pale,_quarta_edizione_del_vocabolario_della_crusca,_1728-39.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
